-- title:
--   r-integrality of ̄ sγ s forces γ∈ sΓ̃ s⁻¹
-- statement:
--   Let $r,\bar r$ be primes with $\bar r\neq r$ and let $N$ be a nonzero squarefree natural number divisible by neither $r$ nor $\bar r$. Let $a_1,b_1\in\mathbb Q$ be such that $B=\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ satisfies `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt` $\bar r$, i.e. $a_1<0$, $b_1<0$ and, for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$, every nonzero element of $B\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ is a unit exactly when $\bar r\in v$. Let $\Lambda_1,R_1\subseteq B$ be $\mathbb Z$-submodules with $\Lambda_1$ a maximal order (an order maximal among the orders containing it), $R_1$ an Eichler order of level $N$ (an intersection of two maximal orders, of relative additive index $N$ in the first), and $R_1\le\Lambda_1$; let $v$ be a height-one prime containing $r$, and let $\Gamma^{t}\le B^{\times}$ be a subgroup whose elements are exactly those of `awayUnits` $R_1\,v$, the intersection over all $w\neq v$ of the preimages under $B^\times\to (B\otimes\mathbb Q_w)^\times$ of the subgroup generated by the local box units of $R_1$ at $w$. Let $\Lambda_1^{s}$ be a further maximal order with $R_1\le\Lambda_1^{s}$ and $\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_1^{s}=R_1$. Let $n_1$ be a unit of $B\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb A_{\mathbb Q}^{\mathrm f}$ lying in `primeHeckeSet` $R_1\,r$ (namely $n_1$ in the finite adelic box of $R_1$, $r\cdot n_1^{-1}$ in that box, while $n_1^{-1}$ and $r^{-1}n_1$ are not), and suppose $\mathrm{meetOrder}\,R_1\,n_1=R_1\cap n_1\widehat{R_1}n_1^{-1}$ is an Eichler order of level $Nr$. Let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell\neq r$ and $\ell\neq\bar r$, let $s\in B^{\times}$ and let $s_f$ be a unit of $B\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb A^{\mathrm f}_{\mathbb Q}$ such that: the component of $s_f$ at every $u$ not containing $r$ is $s\otimes 1$; the component at every $u$ containing $r$ is $1$; the product of the diagonal image of the scalar $\ell$ with $s_f^{-1}$ lies in `levelHeckeUSet` $\Lambda_1\,(\mathrm{meetOrder}\,R_1\,n_1)\,\ell$ when $\ell\mid N$ (that is, in the prime Hecke set of $\mathrm{meetOrder}\,R_1\,n_1$ at $\ell$, with the conjugate of that order by it distinct from it and the order not contained in the conjugate of $\Lambda_1$), and in `primeHeckeSet` $(\mathrm{meetOrder}\,R_1\,n_1)\,\ell$ otherwise; and $\mathrm{nrd}(s)=\ell$. Finally let $\gamma\in\Gamma^{t}$ and assume there are $K\in\mathbb N$ and $y\in\Lambda_1^{s}$ with $r^{K}\,(\bar s\gamma s)=\ell\, y$, where $\bar s=\mathrm{star}\,s$. The conclusion is that $\gamma$ lies in the image of $\Gamma^{t}$ under conjugation by $s$, i.e. $\gamma=s x s^{-1}$ for some $x\in\Gamma^{t}$.
--
--   This is the purely quaternionic half of the stabiliser dictionary attached to the supersingular base point in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation: $r$-integrality of $\bar s\gamma s$ in the twin maximal order $\Lambda_1^{s}$ characterises membership of $\gamma$ in the conjugate $s\tilde\Gamma s^{-1}$ of the away-from-$r$ unit group. It is used in the statement identifying preservation of the extra level structure on the fake elliptic curve with membership in $\tilde\Gamma\cap s\tilde\Gamma s^{-1}$.
